WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.630
A reaction can also appear to lose mass
if a gas escapes from an open container.

00:00:02.544 --> 00:00:03.095
Correct.

00:00:03.401 --> 00:00:04.637
The gas still exists.

00:00:04.869 --> 00:00:06.751
It has left what the balance is weighing.

00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:10.464
A falling reading is not evidence
that atoms were destroyed.

00:00:11.209 --> 00:00:15.001
For an exam, I should explain the
movement of matter across the system

00:00:15.002 --> 00:00:17.747
boundary, not say gases have no mass.

00:00:18.506 --> 00:00:19.228
Precisely.

00:00:19.541 --> 00:00:21.235
These are conceptual diagrams.

00:00:21.617 --> 00:00:24.764
Never seal a heated vessel
or a gas-producing reaction

00:00:24.765 --> 00:00:26.264
to test the idea yourself.

00:00:26.704 --> 00:00:28.182
Pressure can become dangerous.

00:00:28.452 --> 00:00:31.885
School apparatus must be selected
and supervised by the teacher.

00:00:32.688 --> 00:00:36.942
Conservation is about accounting for
matter, not making a risky pressure bottle

00:00:37.286 --> 00:00:41.409
Let us balance hydrogen reacting
with oxygen to form water using

00:00:41.409 --> 00:00:43.455
cards rather than an actual flame.

00:00:44.054 --> 00:00:47.584
Start with H2 + O2 → H2O.

00:00:48.301 --> 00:00:49.097
What is wrong?

00:00:49.937 --> 00:00:53.184
Oxygen has two atoms on the
left and one on the right.

00:00:53.659 --> 00:00:56.425
I could change the water to H2O2.

00:00:57.222 --> 00:00:58.968
Emergency imaginary tissue.

00:01:00.124 --> 00:01:03.609
H2O2 is hydrogen peroxide, not water.

00:01:04.261 --> 00:01:06.653
Changing a subscript
changes the substance.

00:01:07.218 --> 00:01:10.583
Balance by changing coefficients
in front of the correct formulae.

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:16.763
2H2O gives two oxygens on the right,
but now there are four hydrogens there.

00:01:17.539 --> 00:01:17.913
Good.

00:01:18.157 --> 00:01:20.003
Put a two in front of H2 as well.

00:01:20.416 --> 00:01:24.269
Now we have four hydrogen atoms
and two oxygen atoms on each side.

00:01:24.678 --> 00:01:28.178
The smallest whole number
coefficients are two, one, and two.

00:01:28.937 --> 00:01:30.574
We usually leave the one unwritten.

00:01:30.961 --> 00:01:33.390
Count, adjust, recount.

00:01:33.847 --> 00:01:36.175
Never quietly edit the
recipe of the product.

00:01:36.952 --> 00:01:37.741
Exactly.

00:01:38.036 --> 00:01:41.952
It is not enough for the total number
of atoms to match if the types do not.

00:01:42.374 --> 00:01:44.777
You must conserve each element separately.

00:01:45.571 --> 00:01:48.393
Also check that the formulas
are correct before starting.

00:01:49.176 --> 00:01:51.994
Otherwise, I could perfectly
balance the wrong substances.

00:01:52.301 --> 00:01:54.116
A neat answer can still be wrong.

00:01:54.946 --> 00:01:59.050
The balanced equation tells us relative
amounts of particles or formula units.

00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:03.238
It does not say two grams of hydrogen
react with one gram of oxygen.

00:02:03.592 --> 00:02:05.724
Coefficients are not simply gram labels.

00:02:06.474 --> 00:02:08.458
Different atoms have different masses.

00:02:09.104 --> 00:02:12.731
Counting particles and weighing
substances are connected, but

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:14.440
they are not the same calculation.

00:02:14.866 --> 00:02:17.080
Chemists group reactions into families.

00:02:17.392 --> 00:02:18.691
Combustion is burning.

00:02:19.004 --> 00:02:22.935
A substance reacts with oxygen and
transfers energy to its surroundings.

00:02:23.521 --> 00:02:27.257
Complete combustion of methane
produces carbon dioxide and water.

00:02:28.159 --> 00:02:31.971
Oxidation means gaining oxygen
in the version we are learning?

00:02:32.732 --> 00:02:33.209
Yes.

00:02:33.426 --> 00:02:35.393
That is our introductory definition.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:40.984
Rusting is the slow oxidation of iron
and requires both oxygen and water.

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:44.366
Rust is not simply dirt
landing on the surface.

00:02:45.143 --> 00:02:49.189
Reduction must mean losing oxygen,
not shrinking the piece of metal.

00:02:49.899 --> 00:02:50.454
Correct.

00:02:50.963 --> 00:02:56.325
In iron extraction, iron oxide can
lose oxygen as carbon monoxide takes

00:02:56.326 --> 00:02:59.030
that oxygen and becomes carbon dioxide.

00:02:59.675 --> 00:03:03.901
The iron oxide is reduced, and
the carbon monoxide is oxidized.

00:03:04.270 --> 00:03:08.005
More advanced chemistry extends
these definitions using electrons.

00:03:08.766 --> 00:03:10.927
What does thermal decomposition mean?

00:03:11.754 --> 00:03:13.079
Thermal means heat.

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:17.024
Decomposition breaks a compound
into simpler substances.

00:03:17.365 --> 00:03:22.451
For example, heating copper carbonate can
produce copper oxide and carbon dioxide.

00:03:22.804 --> 00:03:26.719
That is different from melting, which
leaves the substance chemically unchanged.

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:29.938
Acid plus base gives salt and water.

00:03:30.314 --> 00:03:34.336
That is neutralization for the
oxide and hydroxide examples in our

00:03:34.337 --> 00:03:34.841
course.

00:03:35.655 --> 00:03:36.453
Exactly.

00:03:36.847 --> 00:03:38.553
Displacement is another family.

00:03:39.148 --> 00:03:42.039
Iron can displace copper
from copper sulfate solution

00:03:42.282 --> 00:03:43.954
because iron is more reactive.

00:03:44.343 --> 00:03:47.303
Iron sulfate forms, and
copper metal is deposited.

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:51.886
A coating is evidence to explain,
not just a color to memorize.

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:56.920
So identifying the family helps
predict the products, but I still need

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:59.154
the actual reactants and conditions

00:03:59.525 --> 00:04:03.984
An exothermic reaction transfers energy
to the surroundings, often heating them.

00:04:04.394 --> 00:04:07.589
An endothermic change takes in
energy from the surroundings.

00:04:07.943 --> 00:04:10.071
Which direction does exothermic mean?

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:12.327
Exo, exit.

00:04:12.866 --> 00:04:14.658
Energy leaves the reacting system.

00:04:14.903 --> 00:04:15.029
It

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:17.098
is transferred, not created.

00:04:17.756 --> 00:04:18.159
Good.

00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:22.211
A temperature rise in a controlled
experiment can support an exothermic

00:04:22.211 --> 00:04:25.823
explanation, while a fall can
support an endothermic one.

00:04:26.196 --> 00:04:29.275
Heat loss, heating equipment,
and other changes affect

00:04:29.302 --> 00:04:31.452
measurements, so context matters.

00:04:32.238 --> 00:04:35.882
A dissolving cold pack substance can
absorb energy even when the lesson

00:04:35.883 --> 00:04:38.247
describes dissolving as a physical change.

00:04:38.784 --> 00:04:40.000
Temperature change alone still
does not prove a new substance.
